WEBVTT

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.870
Just about a year ago when we
had our entrance ceremony...

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.250
"Class 1-A"     "Class 1-B"

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.250
Just about a year ago when we
had our entrance ceremony...

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.330
"Class 1-A"     "Class 1-B"

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.330
Our class assignments were stuck
to the bulletin boards.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.540
Our class assignments were stuck
to the bulletin boards.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.500
And among the crowd of new students,

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:26.080
there was one other girl keeping her distance
from the crowd, just like myself.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.660
The girl who exchanged glances with me then
just happened to be Shimamura.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.910
Of course, back then, I had
absolutely no interest in strangers.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.870
I even hoped that she'd stop looking at me.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:45.160
A year had passed, and now, Shimamura
and I were both second-years.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.580
Does God actually exist?

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:57.120
Was there something that could
hear my voiceless prayer?

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.790
We're in the same class again.
How many years has it been now?

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.290
About ten?

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:05.870
Looks like almost everyone else
got split up. Like Shimamura.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:09.700
If we end up in separate classes,

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:13.950
Shimamura probably wouldn't come to see me.

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:17.410
She probably wouldn't mind
if I came to see her, but...

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.750
But she wouldn't come to see me.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:24.040
Because I don't think Shimamura
actually needs me that badly.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.410
"Class 2-B"
"Sakura Adachi"

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:31.950
I'm definitely not a decent
person worth any praise.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.250
I can't imagine that I've done

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:39.040
enough good deeds to be
rewarded with anything I ask for.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.410
But...

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:43.870
Does God actually exist?

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:47.450
Was there something that could
hear my voiceless prayer?

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.580
"Sakura Adachi"

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.700
I wish and I hope...

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.700
I stand tall, searching for that name...

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:05.580
Yes! Yippee!

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:09.370
Yes! Yippee! Yippee!

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:10.200
Yes!

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.950
"Hogetsu Shimamura"

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.580
I started my second year in high school

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:50.120
and my hair color went
back to its natural color.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.950
In my new class,

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:54.790
my seat and most of my classmates had changed,

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:59.700
but Adachi still remained right in front of me.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.910
So your first name is Sakura?

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.080
Yeah.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.700
Did I ever ask you that before?

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:10.450
Huh? Um, I think so.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.500
Huh...?

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:16.870
Sakura.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.200
Huh?!

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.370
Or do you prefer Miss Sakura?

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.700
What's wrong, Adachi?

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.870
Um...

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:29.700
I-It's nothing...

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:36.290
Er, I mean... Wait, what?

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:39.620
Nothing. I was just looking at you.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:41.540
O-Oh...

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.290
You were looking at me.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:52.870
Adachi... Why are you following me?

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:55.950
Well, I...

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:58.910
What about your bike?

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.620
O-Oh, that's what you meant.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.830
Sh-Shimamura?

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:08.660
You look so much like a puppy sometimes.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.200
Huh?

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.700
Woof.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.750
I do not.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.370
Are you sure?

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.500
I-I'll go get my bike.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.660
I actually like dogs quite a bit, though.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:29.250
I will never get over how big her house is.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:36.080
Roll, roll, roll, roll, roll, roll...

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:37.540
You having fun?

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:40.620
The smell of the tatami is just so...

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:47.410
I changed, just like you asked.
This is what you wanted, right?

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.250
Ooh.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.200
Uh, hey?

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:07.870
You're so cute, Hino.

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:10.160
Wh-Where'd that come from?

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.790
That was the first thought to cross my mind.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.160
Seriously...

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.830
Now, then. I guess I'll get changed, too.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.870
Wait. Changed?

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:21.370
I was planning to spend the night
at your place today.

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:22.870
What? Spend the night?

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:24.580
Well, your place is huge,

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:28.120
so I figured no one would notice
even if I stayed over. Yup.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:31.120
Seriously... You should've asked me first.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.080
Well, you'd object if I did.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.790
So you do know me.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.000
I sure do.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.750
Akira, do you have a moment?

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.950
Oh, you're Tae, aren't you?

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:43.620
Yes, I sure am.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:46.160
Er, your name is Taeko.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.660
What did you need?

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:54.660
I'm glad you're already changed.
Please come greet our guests.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:58.160
What? Why do I have to greet them, too?

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.580
Well, you're a part of this family.

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:04.700
Okay, fine.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:11.290
And this is exactly why
I hate coming home early.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.830
You're Shimamura, right?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.040
Yeah, I am.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:29.410
Great. Hey, wanna have lunch with us?

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:32.080
Huh? I, uh...

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.120
Do you have plans?

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.410
Huh? No, but...

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:41.000
Then, come on. Come sit with us.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.410
O-Okay, I guess?

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:49.830
Yay!

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:51.700
Th-Thanks...?

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:54.370
Come this way, Shimamura.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.540
Uh, okay.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:06.120
Oh, I didn't bring my lunch,
so I'm going to go buy something.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.040
Huh?

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:14.870
Adachi...

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.950
So have you guys been friends for a while?

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:20.950
Nah, just since this year.

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:22.160
I see...

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.750
Are you in any clubs, Shimamura?

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.750
Nope, not at all.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:28.580
Wow, what a surprise.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.410
I'm in concert band.
The number of members is a bit iffy.

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:33.750
They all introduced themselves,

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:36.330
but they talked too fast
and I couldn't understand them.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:42.790
I think it was something like
Pancho, Sancho, and Delos.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:46.870
I figured they must be some kind
of traveling comedy troupe. JK.

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:49.500
There's no way that those
were actually their names.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.750
And then, their idle chatter continued, but...

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:54.910
To be honest,

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:58.080
I tried to remember what they
were talking about, but just couldn't.

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:04.290
Say, Shimamura.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:08.700
We're going to the café by the station now.
Want to come with us?

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.000
Huh?

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:13.910
Their pancakes are super yummy.

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:15.870
It's such a cute little shop.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:17.160
Right?

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.200
What do you say?

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:21.580
Yeah, uh... Sorry, I can't today.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:28.120
Our classes changed and now that
Hino and Nagafuji were gone,

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:31.700
I've made new artificial friends.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:35.080
I mean, Hino and Nagafuji
were at least entertaining.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:37.580
But we weren't so close
I'd go out of my way

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:40.250
to hang out with them now
that our classes were different.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:43.540
Now that I think about it,

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.910
I don't keep up with people.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:51.120
I don't really hold onto relationships
and that might make me coldhearted.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:54.620
But here's how I see it.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:57.750
There are so very few strong relationships

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:00.620
that flow along with you
down this river of life.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:02.330
"When should I return the notes I borrowed?"
"The next time we see each other is fine."

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:03.870
"When should I return the notes I borrowed?"
"The next time we see each other is fine."

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:03.870
The longer you stay in this river of fate,

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.370
"Thanks."
"I haven't seen..."

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.370
The longer you stay in this river of fate,

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:09.290
the more bonds weaken, and eventually break.

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:18.200
Adachi stopped showing up to class

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:21.830
the following Monday after the weekend.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.700
Should I go have a peek?

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:37.790
Maybe that's what Adachi's waiting for.

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:43.830
But if I go up there and a teacher spots us...

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:48.290
By the way, are you close with Adachi?

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:52.080
Y-Yeah, she's my friend.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:57.750
I figured. I saw you two talking all
the time last year. Is she sick today?

00:10:57.750 --> 00:10:59.120
I'm not sure...

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:05.450
So I went to the same middle school
as Adachi, but she's totally changed.

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:06.500
Really?

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:10.290
Yeah. I mean, she still didn't
talk to anyone in class,

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:13.790
but she seemed even more guarded.

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:16.370
I'm not sure if any of that has changed.

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:19.500
Nah, there's something different.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:23.290
She doesn't feel so... standoffish.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:28.450
In other words, she doesn't
seem so prickly anymore.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:31.580
At least, when I interact with Adachi,

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:36.500
she doesn't bother with the thorns
and just stiffens and curls up.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:39.410
Adachi's rejection wasn't even that strong,

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:41.910
but I'm stubborn.

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:43.910
In the end...

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:47.120
I didn't go check the second floor of the gym.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:58.620
"Tarumi"
"Incoming Call"

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:00.750
Tarumi...

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:06.450
Oh, hey... Um, Taru.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.080
Hey, Shima.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.450
So, hey...

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:12.870
Yeah?

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.660
Wanna hang out sometime?

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:18.950
Oh, I'll try harder this time. I mean,

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:21.450
so things don't end up as awkward as last time.

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:24.660
Um, I don't know if you need to...

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:26.540
Um...

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:32.120
Sure. Yeah, we're going to hang out, right?

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:35.580
Yeah. How about next Saturday?

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:36.700
Sure.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:40.540
Yay! Heck yeah! I'm so excited!

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:43.540
U-Um, Miss... Taru?

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:47.040
I figured this was a better attitude to have.

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:50.000
Is that so...

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:53.080
Do you prefer hanging out with someone calmer?

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.080
Say what?

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.540
This is worth looking into...

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:01.910
At least she's decisive about that.

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:07.120
Man, this is paradise...
Having such a big bath is so nice.

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:11.000
I prefer the one at your place.

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:12.660
Wow, you're picky.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:14.500
I'd call it being frugal.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:17.370
I mean, I like smaller houses.

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:20.950
I see, I see. Wanna trade homes then?

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:25.000
Actually... Yeah, that'd be nice.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:29.830
It's not like anything would
change here even if I was gone.

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:57.080
I figured I'd let you touch
them once in a while.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.620
You like them, don't you?

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:00.290
H-Huh?

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:06.000
I'm so generous, aren't I? But don't
move your fingers around too much.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.580
Are you having fun?

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:12.120
Th-That's enough, tha--

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:15.750
You really are cute, Hino.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:20.080
I guess you really do like me.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:21.330
Yup.

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:28.830
What's going to happen once we see each other?
I probably shouldn't think that.

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:33.410
I don't think that when I go out with Adachi.

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:35.870
I'm sure there's a lot going on.

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:41.580
Whoa, you're early!

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:47.750
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:57.910
I guess Adachi's about the only person
who'd rush over in a Chinese dress...

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.080
What's so funny?

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.200
Do I look weird?

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:06.120
Oh, was I laughing?

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:10.290
I was just thinking about a friend.

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:13.950
I see. I'm not late, am I?

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:16.450
Nah, I just came too early.

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:18.080
Thank goodness.

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:23.080
Well, so, uh... Let's do this.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:24.580
What?

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:28.330
Er...

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:32.410
Woo-hoo! Shima!

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.160
Y-Yeah...

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:36.580
Well, let's go!

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.200
Oh... Where are we going?

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.040
It's still a secret.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:56.580
Well?

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:58.370
Say something.

00:15:58.370 --> 00:16:02.080
Um... Oh, right. I just remembered.

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:06.370
You always laughed like that, Taru.

00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:08.870
Shima, you've gotten sexier...

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:12.160
No, wait.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:14.580
Ugh, I can't think of the words...

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:18.580
I think I wanted to say...
You've gotten bigger.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:23.080
Look who's talking.

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:31.000
I really don't think you need to
push this being super excited thing.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:34.910
Don't worry. At least half of it is genuine.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:41.830
"<i>Okonomiyaki</i>"

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:44.000
Hup!

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:50.580
Isn't this exhausting for your face?

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:56.870
But I think stuff like this
is important... Maybe.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:17:00.120
So I hear you've been responsible lately?

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.370
Huh?

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:05.700
Your mom calls my mom sometimes.

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:07.290
That's where I heard that.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:11.370
They only talk to each other
super rarely, though.

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:13.200
They go so long without speaking.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.660
I'd love to hear that from
you personally, though.

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:19.660
That's partially the reason why
I invited you out today.

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:20.910
Wait, my goal?

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:24.790
There has to be a nicer way to say it...

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:33.080
We talked about our recent events while
making sure our <i>okonomiyaki </i>didn't burn.

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:35.910
Taru is surprisingly observant.

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:40.370
If this were Adachi, I spaced out and
imagined she'd probably burn the bottom.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:47.410
That's how much whatever Taru was
saying wasn't getting through to me.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:50.790
I truly am a coldhearted person.

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:52.700
Even though I was physically facing her,

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:56.540
there was still a part of me
keeping its distance.

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:58.120
So basically...

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:00.620
I want to say that you're my acquaintance...

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:02.620
Acquaintance?

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:07.830
That I've known for a while...
And now I'm here in front of you...

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.160
What am I even saying?

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:20.410
So, where are we going next?

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.580
Huh? Um...

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:28.700
Hey, there's a little shop over there.

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:30.410
Maybe they sell random knickknacks.

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:32.870
Y-Yeah...

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:34.910
Why don't we check it out?

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:36.540
Huh?

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:40.120
Hey, they have a lot of straps.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.330
Why don't we buy matching ones?

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:43.750
Sure...

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:48.290
Which one do you like? I'll match mine
with whatever one you pick.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:51.450
Then...

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:54.950
Will you actually put it on your bag?

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:56.950
Is that something to worry about?

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:59.910
I have a feeling you'd lose it immediately.

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:02.290
Jeez, that's rude.

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:06.700
Well, I mean... You don't really
get attached to people or things.

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:10.160
Really?

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:13.540
So I'm worried that you
might not take care of it.

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.290
Then I guess...

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:18.450
I'll take good care of this.

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:21.160
Really?

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:23.870
You really don't trust me.

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:27.330
Because your expression
is really vague right now.

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:30.200
Huh? Vague?

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:35.040
But whenever I see your profile with
such a vague expression on your face

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:38.580
I wonder what you're actually thinking about.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:42.540
But then I lose...

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:47.500
Or maybe I win...

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:53.000
Or something.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:57.700
Well, I'll see you.

00:19:57.700 --> 00:19:59.750
Yeah, see ya.

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:01.750
Um...

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:04.870
Would it be possible to hang out again?

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.410
Sure.

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:17.200
Let's be friends again, Shima!

00:20:20.370 --> 00:20:21.910
I see.

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:26.000
So that's why she invited me out today.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.120
Sure.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:35.200
Ah, Shimamura.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:38.330
I have located Shimamura!

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:41.290
Shimamura!

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:42.750
S-See you later...

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:45.750
Shimamura!

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:47.250
What's the matter?

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:49.700
I'm just a bit tired.

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:58.830
Taru has always been like that, and in
the past, I was able to keep up with her.

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:02.950
Actually, I think that maybe
I'm the odd one out here.

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:09.080
What even am I?

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:12.410
You're just you, Shimamura.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:21.450
I guess you're right.
You actually can be useful at times.

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:23.950
Yes, I know.

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:37.580
--Two weeks after our first term started...
--So, yesterday, I went to club
for the first time in a while.

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:39.790
--As usual, I went to my classes,
bought bread at the student store,
--So, yesterday, I went to club
for the first time in a while.

00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:41.910
--As usual, I went to my classes,
bought bread at the student store,
--That's rare.
--They were awful.

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:44.540
--and ate lunch with my artificial friends.
--Oh, it's that third-year, huh?

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:47.330
--I just kept doing the same thing
over and over.
--Yeah, Yamada.
--Being in a club is sort of a pain.

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:49.500
--The only thing that was different...
--Yeah, Yamada.
--Being in a club is sort of a pain.

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:53.330
--...was Adachi wasn't in front of me.
--They're so annoying.

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:54.950
Relationships are so hard.

00:21:54.950 --> 00:21:56.410
You can say that again.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:22:00.120
By the way, on our way home,
wanna get pancakes again?

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:01.450
Totally!

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:02.950
What about you, Shi--?

00:22:05.540 --> 00:22:07.200
Shimamura.

00:22:10.950 --> 00:22:13.200
After Sancho, and Taru,

00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:16.120
this was the third time someone
called me since April started.

00:22:16.120 --> 00:22:19.250
I guess the third time really is the charm.

00:22:19.250 --> 00:22:21.750
I mean...

00:22:21.750 --> 00:22:25.450
"Episode 10: 'Cherry Blossoms and
Spring and Spring and the Moon'"

00:22:21.750 --> 00:22:25.450
This time, it was finally Adachi.

